|lore=Installed at many facilities throughout the Empire to provide power to the Imperial spacefleet. Supplies starships with energy necessary for sub-light and hyperspace travel.
|game_text=Deploy on a docking bay or your capital starship. Star Destroyers and unique (•) TIEs are immune to attrition < 3. May place this device in Lost Pile to cancel Hyper Escape or Power Pivot. If opponent controls this location, place this device in Used Pile.
|printings={{Card versions/Fusion Generator Supply Tanks (Dark) (Premiere)}}
|versions={{Card versions/Fusion Generator Supply Tanks (Dark) (Premiere)}}
|errata_history=The Players Committee first published this Virtual card on an old-style slip (before its December 2006 remaster of the set). Icons printed on the slip are written here in brackets ([Pilot], [Immune to Alter], [Immune to Sense], [Immune to Control]); ▲ and ▼ are printed as such. Versions of the Virtual Original card, in date order:
* '''Original''' ([[Fusion Generator Supply Tanks (V) (Dark) (Virtual Set 1)]]): the Players Committee's Virtual Set #1a sheet (PDF made 5 March 2002; tournament-legal 9 March 2002). Full text: “Deploy on a docking bay or your capital starship. Star Destroyers and unique (•) TIEs are immune to attrition < 3. May place this card in Lost Pile to cancel Power Pivot or Hyper Escape. Place in Used Pile if opponent controls this location.”
* '''PC-E1''' ([[Fusion Generator Supply Tanks (V) (Dark) (Virtual Set 1) (Errata)]]): the Virtual Set #1 sheet hosted by Decipher (PDF made 6 March 2002; tournament-legal 9 March 2002). Full text: “Deploy on a docking bay or your capital starship. Star Destroyers and unique (•) TIEs are immune to attrition < 3. May place this card in Lost Pile to cancel Power Pivot or Hyper Escape. Place in Used Pile if opponent controls this location.” '''What changed:''' the words are the same as the previous version; the slip's look differs (Decipher's sheet prints Dark Side text boxes black on white and prints collector numbers V1•1–V1•12; the 5 March sheet prints Dark Side boxes white on black and no numbers). Listed as its own version because it is a separate publication (Bill, 12 November 2026).
* '''Numbered white-on-black''' ([[Fusion Generator Supply Tanks (V) (Dark) (Virtual Set 1: Legacy) (Numbered white-on-black)]]): the numbered Virtual Set #1a option has the same wording and values as the [[Fusion Generator Supply Tanks (V) (Dark) (Virtual Set 1) (Errata)|numbered black-on-white option]], with white text on black. Both PDFs record creation on 6 March 2002 and state tournament legality from 9 March. The extra publication is not a new gameplay text state.
* '''PC-E2''' (this page): the Players Committee remaster sheet (Virtual Set 1: Legacy, official text as of 4 December 2006). Full text: “Deploy on a docking bay or your capital starship. Star Destroyers and unique (•) TIEs are immune to attrition < 3. May place this device in Lost Pile to cancel Hyper Escape or Power Pivot. If opponent controls this location, place this device in Used Pile.” '''What changed:''' “card” → “device”; added “Hyper Escape or”; “Pivot or Hyper Escape. Place in Used Pile if” → “Pivot. If”; “location.” → “location, place this device in Used Pile.”.
|sources=* Historical PC full-card image: [https://web.archive.org/web/20071218114419/http://www.swccgpc.com/cards/v1/ds/fusionds.gif Fusion Generator Supply Tanks (Dark)], swccgpc.com (Internet Archive, 18 December 2007).
* Publisher slip and card text: [https://web.archive.org/web/20071024153847/http://www.swccgpc.com/Resources/VirtualCards1.pdf#page=2 VirtualCards1.pdf, page 2, card 11], Players Committee; official text as of 4 December 2006 (Internet Archive, 24 October 2007).
* CardMaker reconstruction recipe: [https://raw.githubusercontent.com/billbisco/swccg-cardmaker/ed271e5000117b80af36bd28e3987c5c34af3ec4/cards/vs1/11.json card 11], billbisco/swccg-cardmaker.
* Lore and art: the printed Decipher card, [[Fusion Generator Supply Tanks (Dark)]].
|hatnote=Earlier versions of this Virtual Original card: [[Fusion Generator Supply Tanks (V) (Dark) (Virtual Set 1)]], [[Fusion Generator Supply Tanks (V) (Dark) (Virtual Set 1) (Errata)]]. For the Decipher card this slip modifies, see [[Fusion Generator Supply Tanks (Dark)]]. Code OVS1 · GEMP id 1101_11.
